644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,1555,5733,1506,553,198,59,26056,10374,13233,90,85,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,488,259,24984,220,18,83,24984,220,16,481,259,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,60,48101,304,264,11031,315,279,1352,400,87,488,379,488,17988,284,294,2418,220,11252,279,11457,6716,4930,66,11991,568,66426,37314,9960,510,27,37420,91339,397,1249,8253,279,11457,6716,1124,1188,66,11,294,10699,8,369,279,11031,23606,17767,87,488,379,488,17988,284,294,57758,429,5610,279,1555,5733,1506,553,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,85,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,488,259,24984,220,18,83,24984,220,16,481,259,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,701,582,1184,311,1477,279,4622,4621,311,279,11031,323,264,1459,389,279,11031,382,5338,11,10542,264,1459,389,279,1555,13,3197,17767,83,284,220,15,59,701,279,1459,374,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,85,25547,15,8,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,24984,220,15,24984,220,16,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,568,2055,11,279,1459,1124,1188,16,11,220,15,11,220,16,10699,8,15448,389,279,11031,382,5847,11,1477,279,5106,4621,315,279,1555,13,576,5106,4621,374,2661,553,279,36829,315,17767,83,57758,304,279,5733,1506,23606,11,892,374,1124,11520,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,24984,220,18,24984,481,16,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,3593,785,4622,4621,311,279,11031,646,387,1730,553,4633,279,5312,1985,315,279,5106,4621,315,279,1555,323,894,4621,429,15448,304,279,11031,13,1205,646,990,279,4621,504,279,1459,1124,1188,16,11,220,15,11,220,16,10699,8,311,2441,1459,389,279,1555,11,1977,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,85,25547,16,8,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,17,24984,220,18,24984,220,15,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,568,576,4621,374,1124,11520,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,17,24984,220,18,24984,220,15,1124,408,90,5187,2555,92,481,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,24984,220,15,24984,220,16,1124,408,90,5187,2555,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,24984,220,18,24984,481,16,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,49555,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,23526,504,279,74003,13,9258,1172,279,41171,13,3155,537,17024,279,6291,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe line parameterized by\n\\[\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\]lies in a plane of the form $x + y + cz = d.$  Enter the ordered pair $(c,d).$\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) for the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\) that contains the line parameterized by \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to find the normal vector to the plane and a point on the plane.\n\nFirst, identify a point on the line. When \\(t = 0\\), the point is \\(\\mathbf{v}(0) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\). So, the point \\((1, 0, 1)\\) lies on the plane.\n\nNext, find the direction vector of the line. The direction vector is given by the coefficients of \\(t\\) in the parameterized equation, which is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nThe normal vector to the plane can be found by taking the cross product of the direction vector of the line and any vector that lies in the plane. We can use the vector from the point \\((1, 0, 1)\\) to another point on the line, say \\(\\mathbf{v}(1) = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The vector is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"92084eefdc3748944f8cc477c0a167c99685897b5547645efea656ebe186152b"},"seconds":47.68205690383911,"seed":15994890039637181,"stop":"eos","text":"Since the direction vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is already aligned with the direction of the line, we need a second vector that is not parallel to this vector but still lies in the plane. We can use another point on the line to find this vector. Let's use \\(t = 1\\) to get the point \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The vector from \\((1, 0, 1)\\) to \\((2, 3, 0)\\) is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nTo find the normal vector to the plane, we need a different point on the line to form a non-parallel vector. Let's use \\(t = -1\\) to get the point \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The vector from \\((1, 0, 1)\\) to \\((0, -3, 2)\\) is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nNow, we can find the normal vector to the plane by taking the cross product of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(3 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-3)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-1)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-3) - 3 \\cdot (-1)) = \\mathbf{i}(3 - 3) - \\mathbf{j}(1 - 1) + \\mathbf{k}(-3 + 3) = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product results in the zero vector, indicating that the vectors are parallel. We can use the given vectors directly to form the plane equation since they are part of the line. The plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\) must be satisfied by the points on the line. Substitute \\((1, 0, 1)\\) into the plane equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + 0 + c \\cdot 1 = d \\implies 1 + c = d\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\((2, 3, 0)\\) into the plane equation:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 + c \\cdot 0 = d \\implies 5 = d\n\\]\n\nSince \\(1 + c = d\\) and \\(d = 5\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n1 + c = 5 \\implies c = 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) is \\(\\boxed{(4, 5)}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(4, 5)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"Since the direction vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is already aligned with the direction of the line, we need a second vector that is not parallel to this vector but still lies in the plane. We can use another point on the line to find this vector. Let's use \\(t = 1\\) to get the point \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The vector from \\((1, 0, 1)\\) to \\((2, 3, 0)\\) is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nTo find the normal vector to the plane, we need a different point on the line to form a non-parallel vector. Let's use \\(t = -1\\) to get the point \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The vector from \\((1, 0, 1)\\) to \\((0, -3, 2)\\) is \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nNow, we can find the normal vector to the plane by taking the cross product of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(3 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-3)) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-1)) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot (-3) - 3 \\cdot (-1)) = \\mathbf{i}(3 - 3) - \\mathbf{j}(1 - 1) + \\mathbf{k}(-3 + 3) = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product results in the zero vector, indicating that the vectors are parallel. We can use the given vectors directly to form the plane equation since they are part of the line. The plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\) must be satisfied by the points on the line. Substitute \\((1, 0, 1)\\) into the plane equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + 0 + c \\cdot 1 = d \\implies 1 + c = d\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\((2, 3, 0)\\) into the plane equation:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 + c \\cdot 0 = d \\implies 5 = d\n\\]\n\nSince \\(1 + c = d\\) and \\(d = 5\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n1 + c = 5 \\implies c = 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) is \\(\\boxed{(4, 5)}\\).","id":"precalculus:264"}
